Production repair for the exact `d9486286...` live blocker where the certifier's first replica bootstrap still asked the 2 GB authoritative service to materialize a ~1.17 GB SQLite snapshot and the cgroup guard correctly failed closed with `MemoryError`.

This changes only certification transport/bootstrap architecture:
- authoritative SQLite remains sole canonical writable store;
- new authenticated logical-bootstrap manifest exposes exact release, replication epoch, full schema fingerprint, starting journal watermark, canonical table DDL and post-schema objects;
- canonical rows are streamed in bounded deterministic keyset pages (rowid for rowid tables; primary-key tuples for WITHOUT ROWID tables);
- every page is release/schema/epoch validated and uses a small SQLite cache with file-cache release after reads;
- mutations racing with the scan are reconciled from the existing append-only replication journal after the local replica is built;
- incremental deltas are now paginated into bounded batches instead of forcing a bootstrap when more than the row cap accumulated;
- certifier catch-up consumes bounded batches until an exact watermark is reached;
- the certifier defaults to logical bootstrap and will not call the full-snapshot transport unless `SOLANA_ROI_CERTIFIER_ALLOW_FULL_SNAPSHOT_BOOTSTRAP` is explicitly enabled for recovery;
- existing full snapshot/chunk/cgroup protection remains available as explicit recovery infrastructure only.

Correctness protections preserved:
- exact release binding;
- schema identity includes tables/columns/views/indexes/user triggers plus schema-version discontinuity;
- stable row identities and WITHOUT ROWID primary-key requirement;
- transactional delta apply, trigger-safe replay, semicolon-safe canonical text;
- fail closed on schema/epoch/release/cursor discontinuity;
- no shared writable disk and no second canonical writer.

No strategy, sizing, entry/exit, wallet economic gate, certification threshold, continuity authority, signing, submission, custody, or live-money changes. Paper-only remains immutable.

Focused tests prove logical schema/row reconstruction without full snapshots, journal repair of mutations racing with the keyset scan, bounded >100-row delta pagination, and full-snapshot bootstrap disabled by default.

Merge only after the complete required CI suite is green on the exact head. Production acceptance then requires both Render services on the exact merge SHA, successful logical bootstrap, multiple consecutive incremental cycles, zero normal-cycle full snapshot requests, no authoritative restart/cgroup MemoryError/SQLite lock recurrence, and fresh exact-release certification surfaces.

