## Block 4 — PHY-11 / PHY-12 browser evidence

Adds scenario-specific Playwright evidence on top of the browser harness merged in PR #77.

Scenario:
- creates an isolated synthetic prepared customer dispatch in the ephemeral CI PostgreSQL database;
- signs in through the real admin login UI;
- opens the Dispatch operations UI;
- verifies the unit and both Enviado/Cancelar controls are visible;
- accepts the real browser confirmation dialog and cancels from UI;
- proves the dispatch leaves the active queue;
- verifies the reserved unit returns to available inventory, reservation ownership is cleared, dispatch item trace remains cancelled, source order remains non-delivered, and the commercial order is detached/reset for fulfillment;
- replays a stale send action from the same authenticated browser context after cancellation;
- expects HTTP 409 and proves no DISPATCHED event/state corruption appears.

Safety:
- all fixture writes occur only in the ephemeral CI PostgreSQL service;
- no production DB writes;
- target transition for PHY-11 is performed from the real UI;
- PHY-12 stale replay uses the authenticated browser context because the cancelled dispatch is intentionally removed from the active UI and no longer offers an Enviado button.

This is evidence for the software/browser portion of PHY-11/12; physical Block 4 gates remain separate.

